                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Absolutely atrocious.\n\nWant to remap the keybindings so it's not the jankiest thing imaginable? Too bad, that doesn't work!\nWant to play the game and fight in the tournaments? Too bad! You need to get money from a stupid repetitive minigame first!\nThink you're gonna win the tournament because the first two rounds were easy? Too bad! Your final opponent randomly has way higher stats!\nThink you're finally piecing him up? Too bad! He executes a perfect block that we didn't teach you how to do!\nThink you're winning on points? Too bad! He randomly injures you and you have no idea how to stop it!\nWant to increase your stats to win tournaments? Too bad! You have to win tournaments to be able to train!\nWant to know what the kicks are? You better be a real karate practitioner, because they're all in Japanese!\nWant to throw a fun combo? Too bad! You're doing a spin kick now!\nWant to enjoy some kind of story? Too bad! It's the most generic thing imaginable!\n\nI've played through the entire story, dragging myself through every infuriating minigame and horribly programmed control, hoping that there would be some kind of light at the end of the tunnel.\n\nThere wasn't. I don't see how even karate fanatics could enjoy this. I don't understand why it has so many positive reviews. This game is legitimately horribly designed, horribly programmed, horribly written, and horribly overrated. I wish I could get my 12 hours back.",
